    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Photographs taken of terra-cotta tiles with simulated parrotfish divots after being out in the field for three years. 10 of the tiles were caged and 10 were un-caged. Each zip file contains 10 photos of an individual tile.  One is the whole view of the tile followed by close ups of each of four quadrates.  Each of the 5 photos are saved in both .JPG and .CR2 (Canon raw 2) formats.  Photos were taken in the lab with a Canon EOS Rebel SL1.\r\n\r\nfile names for the photos are: site&depth.YYMMDD.tile#&treatment.photo#.photo coverage\r\n\r\nFR9S.140623.1C.2632.W = FR9, shallow, 6/23/14, tile 1, caged, number assigned by the camera, whole plate\r\n\r\n• sites are FR3, FR7, FR9 (FR stands for fore-reef)\r\n• depths are S=shallow, M=middle, D=deep\r\n• dates are formatted as YYMMDD, for example 140623 is June 23, 2014\r\n• tile numbers as written on the tiles\r\n• treatments are C=caged, U=uncaged\r\n• photo# is number assigned by the camera\r\n• photo coverages are:\r\n    W=whole plate, A=upper right, B=lower right, C=lower left, D=upper left\r\n    this is with the tile oriented so divot #1 is in upper right (A)",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Micheli, F., McCauley, D., and Wible, J. (2023). Benthic recruitment tile images from Palmyra Atoll 2016. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/xb648zm1912. https://doi.org/10.25740/xb648zm1912.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
